# "If an activated or triggered ability of a permanent ... tries to transform it, the permanent does so only if it hasn't
# transformed ... since the ability was put onto the stack" (CR 701.27f; Ashling's ruling names this case). Delney,
# Streetwise Lookout makes Ashling's (power 1) "at the beginning of your first main phase, you may pay {U}. If you do,
# transform Ashling" trigger an additional time on turn 5. The first is paid with the Island and Ashling transforms;
# Ashling, Rimebound's "whenever this creature transforms into Ashling, Rimebound" triggers twice too (Delney), adding
# {B}{B} twice. The second is then paid with Mox Sapphire, but Ashling has transformed since that ability was put on
# the stack, so it stays Ashling, Rimebound - it does not turn back, and Rekindled's rummage never triggers.

